1
00:00:03,109 --> 00:00:04,674
The fish opens and closes

2
00:00:04,724 --> 00:00:06,161
its mouth all the time.

3
00:00:06,211 --> 00:00:07,130
Is it drinking?

4
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:07,324
No!

5
00:00:07,374 --> 00:00:09,845
Mila sees the slits moving on its side.

6
00:00:09,895 --> 00:00:10,814
It's breathing…

7
00:00:10,864 --> 00:00:12,092
but breathing what?

8
00:00:12,871 --> 00:00:15,771
There is oxygen in the water, invisible,

9
00:00:15,821 --> 00:00:17,984
dissolved like sugar in juice.

10
00:00:18,034 --> 00:00:20,197
The tiny bubbles on the glass?

11
00:00:20,247 --> 00:00:20,689
Proof!

12
00:00:21,462 --> 00:00:22,976
Discovery mission!

13
00:00:25,492 --> 00:00:26,145
Mini mode!

14
00:00:26,195 --> 00:00:28,466
In the air, oxygen is everywhere.

15
00:00:28,516 --> 00:00:30,928
In water, there is much less of it:

16
00:00:30,978 --> 00:00:34,002
you need a special tool to catch it: gills!

17
00:00:34,829 --> 00:00:37,352
The fish swallows water and pushes it over its gills:

18
00:00:37,402 --> 00:00:39,344
thousands of red filaments full of blood.

19
00:00:39,394 --> 00:00:40,946
The oxygen passes into the blood,

20
00:00:40,996 --> 00:00:42,793
the water goes out through the slits.

21
00:00:43,770 --> 00:00:47,008
Out of the water, the filaments stick together and dry out:

22
00:00:47,058 --> 00:00:48,122
the fish suffocates.

23
00:00:48,172 --> 00:00:49,516
For us it's the opposite:

24
00:00:49,566 --> 00:00:51,850
our lungs can't take oxygen out of water.

25
00:00:52,675 --> 00:00:53,232
Up close:

26
00:00:53,282 --> 00:00:56,805
the water slides over the gills like over a red comb.

27
00:00:56,855 --> 00:00:59,300
And who puts the oxygen in the water?

28
00:00:59,350 --> 00:01:00,833
Tiny plants: plankton!

29
00:01:01,628 --> 00:01:03,889
That's how fish breathe underwater.

30
00:01:05,128 --> 00:01:06,753
Fish catch the oxygen hidden

31
00:01:06,803 --> 00:01:08,598
in the water with their gills.

32
00:01:10,111 --> 00:01:12,323
With an adult, in front of an aquarium:

33
00:01:12,373 --> 00:01:17,362
count how many times the fish opens its mouth in one minute, and watch its slits move!

34
00:01:18,151 --> 00:01:20,016
And why are bubbles round?

35
00:01:20,066 --> 00:01:21,539
The answer tomorrow.
